            <div xml:id="d851">

                <pb facs="0946" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg844"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/762: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-14T16:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1919,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 16,
                            12.40 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Consular Agent Saxe reports increasing aggravated conditions in Puntarenas,
                    including forcible search by soldiers of one American home and an American
                    seaman robbed of $40 by Tinoco soldiers. <pb facs="0947" n="845" xml:id="pg845"
                    /> Also continued fighting on the Nicaraguan frontier. He suggests, and I
                    strongly recommend sending naval vessel Puntarenas, at least for time. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Castine</hi> must go to Colon for repairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
